  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WRI-Enhance saving water resources</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Hanoi - the second most populated city in Vietnam with an average number of 8.330.000 people estimated in 2021 along with burgeoning population, is currently dealing with the high demand of water usage. Considering such issue of water resources scarcity in the urban area, especially in big city like Hanoi, the Water Resources Institution (WRI) has proposed an initiative to enhance the effectiveness of regulations implementation regarding water usage efficiency in daily life by improving the understandingof water resourcesvalue and measures in saving and reusing water in daily life for students from primary to high school level in Hanoi. By targeting the beneficiary as students, the project aims to form a good behavior in efficient usage of water among students at their early age which can creates a long-term impact towards their practices in using water and disseminate such messages to schools, family, and their living residential area. The project selects to conduct pilot at 03 inter-levels schools: Experimental Science Education School;Lomonosov West Hanoi Schools; and The Dewey Schools. Through the design of digital programme for providing knowledge and the construction of interactive game (e-Prowater) for students in 3 targeted schools regarding water resources value, the project aims to reach and raise awareness for 1050 children, 600 women (including teacher and mothers) and 400 teachers as well as fathers. Besides, by conducting research and analysis activities, the initiative intent to contribute ideas and advice to the Department of Water Resources Management on the current situation of domestic water use in Hanoi and measures to save water and reuse water in potential daily activities.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">European Union</narrative>
  </participating-org>
  <participating-org role="4" type="80">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institute of Water Resources Scienc</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Water Resources Institution (WRI) - a subordinate unit of the Ministry of Natural Resources and Environment (MONRE) &#x2013; was officially established under the virtue of Prime Minister&#x2019;s Decision No.1896/QD-TTg dated November 28th, 2017 along with the Decision No.838/QD-BTNMT on March 16th, 2018 of the MONRE regulating the functions, missions, authority and organizational structure of the WRI. WRI is a science and technology organization with the functions of basic research, specifically on economy, policy and models in water resource management, distribution, utilization and preservation; water resources technological application and development for state management; consultancy service regarding water resources issue. The guiding principles of the Institute are transparency, efficiency, respect and good cooperation with stakeholders. The Institute&apos;s future development plan orientation is to continue to successfully complete the tasks assigned by the Government, simultaneously expand cooperation with Governmental and Non-governmental organizations to implement domestic and foreign projects. Furthermore, the mission of the Institute is to provide high quality consulting services to support socio-economic development and contribute to the betterment of the management of water resources in particularand environmental management in general. Such orientation demonstrates the stability and independence of the Institution through participating in development activities appropriate to local circumstances.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
